# `std/io/db/sqlite`

```hql
module io.db.sqlite
```

SQLite: one table of a database file, as a transport read by `source`
and `tap` and written by `target` like any other endpoint (module `io`).
The `sqlite` kind of a configured endpoint is this transport under an
id, with a schema boundary. A program imports the module:
`import io.db.sqlite`.

- [`Sqlite`](types/Sqlite.hmd) — One table of an SQLite database file.
- [`sqlite`](sqlite.hmd) — The table `table` of the database file at `path`, as a `Sqlite` transport; its parameters are the keys of the `sqlite` kind.
<!-- hql reference: end -->
